From 8a9732a83042fe0a3558e5176dff540bdead79c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Md Arif <111168803+sabamdarif@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 02:37:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 0043-preload-libsofficeapp-for-bionic-rtti-unification

Fixes the white Start Center window. Root cause chain confirmed live on
device (LineageOS 13 / Bionic, aarch64):

- The 0041 RTTI-DIAG instrumentation fired with a ucb::NameClashException
  whose type_info lived in libucpfile1.so (0x7283ff1468) while the catch
  site's uno::Exception type_info lived in libsofficeapp.so (0x7555718fe8).
- Reading the live process memory showed libucpfile1's whole exception
  base chain (NameClashException -> io::IOException -> uno::Exception)
  bound to its OWN local copies, despite 0042's promotion reporting 42
  libraries promoted. No DT_SYMBOLIC involved.
- A minimal two-library experiment on the device (weak type_info + weak
  data duplicated in liba/libb, libb dlopen'd later) established Bionic's
  actual semantics:
    * liba RTLD_LOCAL, then RTLD_NOLOAD|RTLD_GLOBAL promotion (0042's
      mechanism): libb still binds its own copies. Typed catch misses.
    * liba dlopen'd RTLD_GLOBAL from the start: same failure.
    * liba as DT_NEEDED of the executable: same failure.
    * liba LD_PRELOADed: libb binds liba's copies; typed catch matches.
  Only the DF_1_GLOBAL flag applied AT LOAD TIME via LD_PRELOAD (or a
  library linked with -Wl,-z,global) affects how later dlopen groups
  resolve these symbols. dlopen-based promotion is a silent no-op.

Fix: export LD_PRELOAD=$sd_prog/libsofficeapp.so in the soffice wrapper.
Components then bind the common UNO exception type_infos to
libsofficeapp's copies -- the same ones the desktop/framework catch sites
use -- restoring pointer-identity catch matching.

Verified on device: Start Center renders fully (screenshot-confirmed),
--writer opens a document, RTTI-DIAG and UNO-RTTI-FABRICATE are silent,
and the NameClashException no longer even escapes: it was always an
internally-handled exception that only surfaced because typed catches
could not match.

Note for a future rebuild: linking all LibreOffice libraries with
-Wl,-z,global should generalize this fix to component<->component
exception types not covered by libsofficeapp's symbol set, and would
remove the LD_PRELOAD requirement.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 desktop/scripts/soffice.sh | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh b/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh
index 7188f393e..b3f5852bb 100755
--- a/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh
+++ b/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh
@@ -53,6 +53,25 @@ cd "$sd_dirname" || exit $?
 sd_prog=$(pwd)
 cd "$sd_cwd" || exit $?
 
+# Termux/Bionic: unlike glibc, Bionic's dynamic linker resolves weak
+# (vague-linkage) symbols per dlopen group, not process-wide. Every dlopen'd
+# UNO component therefore binds the C++ exception type_info objects
+# (_ZTIN3com3sun4star...) to its own local copy, and because libc++abi
+# matches catch clauses by type_info pointer identity, UNO exceptions thrown
+# in one .so escape every typed catch in another .so (observed as the
+# startup abort / white Start Center window).
+#
+# Preloading libsofficeapp.so force-sets DF_1_GLOBAL on it at load time,
+# which is the ONLY mechanism Bionic honors for placing a library's symbols
+# ahead of a later dlopen group's own copies: on-device tests show that both
+# dlopen(RTLD_GLOBAL) at load time and later RTLD_NOLOAD|RTLD_GLOBAL
+# "promotion" do NOT affect how subsequently loaded libraries bind these
+# symbols, but LD_PRELOAD does. With this, every component binds the
+# exception type_info base chain to libsofficeapp's copies and typed
+# catches match again.
+LD_PRELOAD="$sd_prog/libsofficeapp.so${LD_PRELOAD:+:$LD_PRELOAD}"
+export LD_PRELOAD
+
 # linked build needs additional settings
 if [ -e "${sd_prog}/ooenv" ] ; then
     # shellcheck source=../../instsetoo_native/ooenv
-- 
2.55.0

